  "source": "# writ.yaml, written by `writ init`. Every tool call your agents make is\n# checked against this file before it runs, and every decision is\n# recorded in a tamper-evident ledger (`writ log`, `writ verify`).\n#\n# default: what happens to a call no rule names. `allow` keeps agents fast;\n# `ask` makes you approve everything the rules below do not decide.\nversion: 1\ndefault: allow\n\n# Bundled policy packs. `floor`: the disasters no agent should cause on its\n# own (wiping ~ or /, force-pushing main, reading SSH/cloud keys, disabling\n# its own hooks); `secrets-guard`: keys and tokens stay out of the model.\n# More: aws-safety, gcp-azure-safety, github-safety, database-safety,\n# k8s-prod, terraform-safety, package-publish-guard, pii-redaction.\npacks: [floor, secrets-guard]\n\n# Your own rules; first match wins, and the packs' deny/ask rules come\n# first. Try one: writ test \"git push --force origin main\"\nrules: []\n"
